{"year":"2024","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"The 77th edition was held on February 18, 2024, at the Royal Festival Hall in London, hosted by David Tennant. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 872585, 'screen_type': movie}\">Oppenheimer</a> (2023) led the nominations, with 13, and won seven awards, including Best Film, as well as Best Director for <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 525, 'screen_type': person}\">Christopher Nolan</a> and Best Leading Actor for <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 2037, 'screen_type': person}\">Cillian Murphy</a>. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 467244, 'screen_type': movie}\">The Zone of Interest</a> (2023) became the first film to win both Outstanding British Film and Best Film Not in the English Language in the same year."},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Picture","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":872585,"name":"Oppenheimer","image_path":"/dUPQszWoRSE9FucJTbVp2bwEi9G.jpg","director":"Christopher Nolan","winner":true,"backdrop_path":"/neeNHeXjMF5fXoCJRsOmkNGC7q.jpg"},{"type":"movie","id":915935,"name":"Anatomy of a Fall","image_path":"/woXYl0DJTx6TsfYWPkSfNHTsoOx.jpg","director":"Justine Triet","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":840430,"name":"The Holdovers","image_path":"/ek4FmIkKlH30xthKs2ANqrV7SOI.jpg","director":"Alexander Payne","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":466420,"name":"Killers of the Flower Moon","image_path":"/kBLMPD5BCmcrHKIhjZ86uWHZG5K.jpg","director":"Martin Scorsese","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":792307,"name":"Poor Things","image_path":"/iOdcXYSVzBgmBJzNIlIMOZ6fz0F.jpg","director":"Yorgos Lanthimos","winner":false}]},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Outstanding British Film","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":467244,"name":"The Zone of Interest","image_path":"/iQoyDhBjHwo1HTR0DuTzR8o1CqI.jpg","director":"Jonathan Glazer","winner":true,"backdrop_path":"/pnTSOKcYnvdpQNQElAtJM1rWOxH.jpg"},{"type":"movie","id":994108,"name":"All of Us Strangers","image_pa